§ `Traces: the duties of the provider`

-- Each rule is a MUST with no time limit and no consequence the text states, except (f), whose time limit is "prior to its being placed on the market or put into service".
-- The act done: FULFILLED. A quiet trace of a rule with no time limit leaves the duty standing (a residual, never BREACH): see NOTES.md "Rules with no breach path (P3)".
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 16(a) the provider's duty to ensure that the high-risk AI system is compliant with the requirements set out in Section 2` (Date 2 12 2027) `P3 Annex III system placed 2 December 2027` `P3 plain circumstances` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Provider DOES `Art 16(a) ensure that the high-risk AI system is compliant with the requirements set out in Section 2` AT 5
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `Art 16(a) the provider's duty to ensure that the high-risk AI system is compliant with the requirements set out in Section 2` (Date 2 12 2027) `P3 Annex III system placed 2 December 2027` `P3 plain circumstances` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 400
-- Day before the date of application: nothing is owed, so even a long wait does not leave a duty standing.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 16(a) the provider's duty to ensure that the high-risk AI system is compliant with the requirements set out in Section 2` (Date 1 12 2027) `P3 Annex III system placed 2 December 2027` `P3 plain circumstances` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 400
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
